<title>USA: KOCH raises U.S. posted crude prices $1.00/BBL.</title>
<headline>KOCH raises U.S. posted crude prices $1.00/BBL.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by $1.00 a barrel, effective today.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $24.75 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $22.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $24.75 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $24.75.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk +1 212 859-1620</p>
</text>
